// What the raster path's stages share: the frame block, the scene's binding group, what a vertex hands a pixel, and the targets.
//
// A module rather than the pipeline file's own, because a material's pixel shader, generated and compiled at run time, lists the same groups and writes the same targets.
// libs/graphics/shaped-viewer/docs/raster.md is the design.
module raster

use tracer

/// The per-frame constants of a raster frame, which `sv::raster_routine` fills.
///
/// The records it holds are the tracer's, so a camera, a light or an instance reaches both paths as the same bytes.
struct frame_constants:
    /// the pinhole camera the image is projected through, as the tracer's primary rays leave it
    camera: tracer.camera_record
    /// the camera of this layer's previous frame, which the motion target reprojects into
    previous_camera: tracer.camera_record
    /// where the projection's depth starts: a pinhole's point at view depth `d` tests at `near_plane / d`, reversed, and writes `1 - near_plane / d` as its primary depth
    /// (`scene.camera_reversed_depth` and `scene.camera_primary_depth`, which an orthographic camera makes linear up to its far plane)
    near_plane: float
    /// how many lights `drawn.lights` holds
    light_count: uint
    /// how many decals `drawn.decals` holds
    decal_count: uint
    /// The angle one pixel spans at the image's center, in radians: a point's footprint is `pixel_width` plus this times its distance.
    pixel_spread: float
    /// The width one pixel spans at the image plane, in meters: an orthographic camera's footprint, which is its whole; 0 for a pinhole.
    pixel_width: float
    /// the image's size in pixels
    size: float2
    /// How far this frame's samples sit from the pixels' centers, in pixels: 0 but where a frame is drawn for an upscaler.
    /// The tracer's `jitter` minus one half, so pixel `px` sees the image at `px + 0.5 + jitter`, where its ray would.
    jitter: float2
    /// The previous frame's `jitter`, where the samples a history was gathered from sat.
    previous_jitter: float2
    /// 0 cuts coverage below one half; anything else seeds a cut drawn per pixel and frame, which frames accumulated converge to the partial surface.
    coverage_seed: uint

/// The scene a raster frame draws — group 0, before the manager's bindless tables at 1 and `slug.tables` at 2.
///
/// Every buffer is the tracer's member of the same name byte for byte, so a layer switching between the two uploads the same records.
binding drawn:
    /// One element, the frame constants.
    frame: buffer[frame_constants]

    /// The per-item table; one draw is one row of it, its first instance.
    instances: buffer[tracer.instance_record]

    /// Every light of the layer, `light_count` of them.
    lights: buffer[tracer.light_record]

    /// The environment, `sv::background_gpu` byte for byte: its 16 SH lanes, then a dome's.
    background: buffer[float4]

    /// The decals every pixel is painted with, `decal_count` of them, and the shapes they cover in the atlas bound as `slug.tables`.
    decals: buffer[tracer.decal_record]
    decal_shapes: buffer[tracer.decal_shape]

/// What the vertex stage hands the pixel stage: which instance, and where on it, in its own space and in the world.
///
/// The draw is indexed, so a corner is shared by the triangles meeting there and cannot say which triangle it is.
/// The pixel stage takes its triangle from `@primitive_id` and finds the barycentrics of `object` in it, which is what a traced hit reports.
struct varyings:
    @position position: hpos4
    /// the row of `drawn.instances`, which the vertex stage takes from `@first_instance`, so a pixel indexes by it unmarked
    @per_draw instance: uint
    /// the point in the mesh's own space, where the barycentrics are found: the corners are stored there, and it is near the origin
    object: float3
    world: float3

/// What a quadric's box hands the pixel stage: `varyings`, and which primitive of the batch the box bounds.
///
/// A box is no surface: the pixel solves the primitive along its own camera ray, and `object` and `world` only say where the box was crossed.
struct quadric_varyings:
    @position position: hpos4
    /// the row of `drawn.instances`, as `varyings` holds it
    @per_draw instance: uint
    /// the primitive of the batch, which the draw takes from `@instance_index`, one instance per box
    @interpolate(.flat) primitive: uint
    object: float3
    world: float3

/// What a raster frame writes per pixel: the lit image and the primary hit's G-buffer.
///
/// Each target is the layer's slot of the same meaning (`sv::impl::raster_slots`, view/view_data.hh), in the format the tracer writes it in.
/// A pixel no surface covers holds the environment in `color`, its reprojection in `motion`, 1 in `primary_depth`, and zero in every other target.
@pixel struct targets:
    /// radiance, and its luminance squared in alpha, `pt.moment_of`, which the mean blends into its second moment
    @format(.rgba32_float) color: float4
    /// the geometric normal turned toward the viewer, in world space
    @format(.rgba16_float) normal: float4
    /// the linear view depth along the camera's forward axis
    @format(.r32_float) depth: float
    /// diffuse reflectance, `openpbr.pt_diffuse_albedo`
    @format(.rgba16_float) albedo: float4
    /// specular reflectance at normal incidence, `openpbr.pt_specular_albedo`
    @format(.rgba16_float) specular_albedo: float4
    /// the sharpest specular lobe's perceptual roughness, `openpbr.pt_roughness`
    @format(.r16_float) roughness: float
    /// this pixel minus where its surface sat on the previous frame's image, in pixels
    @format(.rg32_float) motion: float2
    /// the clip depth, `1 - near_plane / depth`, which a layer's drawings are occluded by
    @format(.r32_float) primary_depth: float

/// `targets` and the depth of the quadric surface a pixel found, which the box it was drawn through does not have.
///
/// The box's far side is drawn, so the surface in front of it only ever raises the reversed depth, which `.greater_equal` promises.
@pixel struct quadric_targets:
    @format(.rgba32_float) color: float4
    @format(.rgba16_float) normal: float4
    @format(.r32_float) depth: float
    @format(.rgba16_float) albedo: float4
    @format(.rgba16_float) specular_albedo: float4
    @format(.r16_float) roughness: float
    @format(.rg32_float) motion: float2
    @format(.r32_float) primary_depth: float
    /// `near_plane / depth`, the raster pass's own reversed depth, at the surface
    @depth(.greater_equal) surface_depth: float
